WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.507
Your kiln breaks.

00:00:02.507 --> 00:00:05.271
Saturday's class is cancelled.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:09.928
Every guest needs a choice, and you still have a studio to run.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.581
Mina bought two tickets.

00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:17.660
Her sister can come Sunday; Mina needs a refund.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:25.975
Raincheck reads the reply, checks the last Sunday place, and proposes one rebooking plus sixty-eight dollars back.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.739
You review the plan and run it.

00:00:29.739 --> 00:00:33.252
Here, the payment response is interrupted.

00:00:33.252 --> 00:00:35.910
The Sunday seat stays held.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:41.344
Reload the desk, recover the saved refund, and the same booking finishes.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:47.362
The outcome gives you a refund reference and a customer reply to send.

00:00:47.362 --> 00:00:50.652
Mina's sister has Sunday's final seat.

00:00:50.652 --> 00:00:53.336
Mina's ticket is refunded.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.244
Other guests have different plans.

00:00:57.244 --> 00:01:00.849
Jules moves both tickets to next Saturday.

00:01:00.849 --> 00:01:04.994
Priya gets a specific question with the available times.

00:01:04.994 --> 00:01:09.362
The ledger keeps settled bookings and open questions together.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.803
Try Raincheck with this fictional workshop.

00:01:13.803 --> 00:01:18.330
The preview uses simulated payments and recorded AI.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.593
Run a small studio?

00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:26.251
Tell us how you handle one cancellation, and explore a twenty-nine-dollar pilot.
